A||||4||Mach10||Wheel bearings||||10||
Z||000000||Mach10||06-07-2001||11:52 PM||||86 SE v6... Left front is making a little noise, all the usual symptoms. <BR>On a scale of 1-10, 1 being changing the air-freshner, and 10 shoe-horning a Jaguar v12 into the engine compartment, AND assuming I have the tools necessary, how difficult is this maintenance? <BR>How much time would I be looking at? Estimates/experience/horror stories welcome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||SteveJ||06-08-2001||08:37 AM||||10 minute job if the bearing raceways are in good condition. A little longer if you hve to chase for a new rotor because of a chewed up raceway. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroluke||06-08-2001||10:05 AM||||It's not difficult at all, but make sure you tighten the bearing(s) just right! It's a good idea to check tightness after a few days, or you may ruin the new set of bearings quickly.<P>------------------<BR>Visit my website: <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  for lots of technical and other Fiero related information<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fieros.de/jpg/th_88gt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||PAUL88GT||06-08-2001||12:25 PM||||It's not too difficult, but it is a dirty job since you have to repack the bearings and hub with grease.  This is also a good time to replace the brake pads since you have to remove the brake calipers to remove the rotors.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||06-09-2001||04:06 PM||||Hee-Hee! The brakes had just been done 3 weeks ago... D-Oh! <BR>Ah well, I'll just find a spare saturday, and do it then. The noise isn't too loud, just a whirring for now, so it should be ok for another 2 weeks until my other job term expires, and I actually have some <I>spare time</I>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||6
